{"nodes": [{"id": "generate_api_auth_spec", "label": "OpenAPI Auth Spec Generator", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "docs/static/frigate-api.yaml is generated, not hand-maintained, so it stays complete and current; exempt lists are read from the auth dependency closure instead of duplicated so the generator cannot drift from frigate/api/auth.py."}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec_build_app", "label": "build_app", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def build_app", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Mirrors the router set of frigate.api.fastapi_app but omits the global admin dependency and runtime state, since only the route table and per-route dependencies are needed for classification."}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec_read_exempt_rules", "label": "read_exempt_rules", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def read_exempt_rules", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reads EXEMPT_PATHS/EXEMPT_PREFIXES out of the require_admin_by_default closure via inspect.getclosurevars rather than copying them, keeping the generator automatically in sync."}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec__route_markers", "label": "_route_markers", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def _route_markers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec__first_segment", "label": "_first_segment", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def _first_segment", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec__handler_enforces_camera", "label": "_handler_enforces_camera", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def _handler_enforces_camera", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Many handlers call require_camera_access inside the body, which dependency introspection cannot see, so the check is recovered from __code__.co_names bytecode. Known ceiling: a call hidden behind a helper function would be missed."}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec_classify_route", "label": "classify_route", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def classify_route", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Promotes an 'any authenticated' route to camera-scoped when the handler enforces per-camera access in its body; admin and public are left alone because for admin the role is the binding requirement and the camera check is only defensive."}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec__classify_base", "label": "_classify_base", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def _classify_base", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Effective access is the intersection of route-level markers and the global secure-by-default admin dependency: a route declaring allow_any_authenticated or allow_public on a non-exempt path is reported as admin, because admin is what actually gets enforced."}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec_build_access_map", "label": "build_access_map", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def build_access_map", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec_security_for", "label": "security_for", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def security_for", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "AUTHENTICATED and CAMERA both map to the user scheme; camera scoping is conveyed via the access note and x-required-role because OpenAPI security cannot express per-resource scoping."}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec_required_role_value", "label": "required_role_value", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def required_role_value", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec_annotate_description", "label": "annotate_description", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def annotate_description", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec_base_document", "label": "base_document", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def base_document", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Blanks info.title deliberately: a docusaurus-openapi-docs convention that suppresses the generated API introduction page."}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec_enrich", "label": "enrich", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def enrich", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec_strip_volatile_defaults", "label": "strip_volatile_defaults", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def strip_volatile_defaults", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Epoch-like numeric defaults (datetime.now() baked in at import time) make the export non-deterministic and document a meaningless frozen epoch, so they are stripped. Noted proper fix: default those route params to None and resolve 'now' in the handler."}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec_to_block_scalars", "label": "to_block_scalars", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def to_block_scalars", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Renders multi-line strings as YAML literal blocks for readable, deterministic diffs instead of long escaped double-quoted lines."}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec_validate", "label": "validate", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def validate", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec_render", "label": "render", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def render", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec_build_spec", "label": "build_spec", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def build_spec", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec_main", "label": "main (auth spec generator entrypoint)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def main", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec__check", "label": "_check", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def _check", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CI guard mode: exits non-zero with a truncated unified diff when the committed spec is stale, so contributors see exactly what regeneration would change."}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec__report", "label": "_report", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def _report", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "generate_api_auth_spec_access_levels", "label": "API Access Level Taxonomy (public/any/camera/admin)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "PUBLIC/AUTHENTICATED/CAMERA/ADMIN constants", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Four ordered access levels emitted as x-required-role plus a bold 'Access:' note per operation, so both machine readers and rendered docs carry the auth requirement."}], "edges": [{"source": "generate_api_auth_spec_main", "target": "generate_api_auth_spec_build_spec", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def main", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "generate_api_auth_spec_main", "target": "generate_api_auth_spec_validate", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def main", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "generate_api_auth_spec_main", "target": "generate_api_auth_spec_render", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def main", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "generate_api_auth_spec_main", "target": "generate_api_auth_spec__check", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def main", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "generate_api_auth_spec_main", "target": "generate_api_auth_spec__report", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.py", "source_location": "def main", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "generate_api_auth_spec_build_spec", "target": "generate_api_auth_spec_build_app", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "generate_api_auth_spec.p